1
00:04:55,000 --> 00:05:01,000
Her legend begins.

2
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:56,000
Tomb Raider is a action, adventure, fantasy film directed by Roar Uthaug.

3
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:51,000
Lara Croft, the fiercely independent daughter of a missing adventurer, must push herself beyond
her limits when she finds herself on the island where her father disappeared.

4
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:46,000
Lara Croft, played by Alicia Vikander.

5
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:41,000
Richard Croft, played by Dominic West.

6
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:36,000
Mathias Vogel, played by Walton Goggins.

7
00:34:25,000 --> 00:34:31,000
Lu Ren, played by Daniel Wu.

8
00:39:20,000 --> 00:39:26,000
Ana Miller, played by Kristin Scott Thomas.

9
00:44:15,000 --> 00:44:21,000
Mr. Yaffe, played by Derek Jacobi.

10
00:49:10,000 --> 00:49:16,000
Tomb Raider is a 2018 action-adventure film directed by Roar Uthaug, with a screenplay by Geneva
Robertson-Dworet and Alastair Siddons, from a story by Evan Daugherty and Robertson-Dworet.

11
00:54:05,000 --> 00:54:11,000
An American and British co-production, it is based on the 2013
video game, with some elements of its sequel.

12
00:59:00,000 --> 00:59:06,000
It is a reboot, and is the third film in the Tomb Raider film series.

13
01:03:55,000 --> 01:04:01,000
The film stars Alicia Vikander as Lara Croft, who embarks on a perilous journey to her
father's last-known destination, hoping to solve the mystery of his disappearance.

14
01:08:50,000 --> 01:08:56,000
Dominic West, Walton Goggins, Daniel Wu, and Kristin
Scott Thomas appear in supporting roles.

15
01:13:45,000 --> 01:13:51,000
Principal photography took place from January to June 2017 at Warner Bros.

16
01:18:40,000 --> 01:18:46,000
Studios, Leavesden in Hertfordshire, England, and Cape Town, South Africa.

17
01:23:35,000 --> 01:23:41,000
The film was also shot on location across London, particularly East London.

18
01:28:30,000 --> 01:28:36,000
The first Tomb Raider film not to be distributed by Paramount Pictures, it was released in the United
Kingdom on March 14, 2018, and in the United States on March 16, 2018, by Warner Bros.

19
01:33:25,000 --> 01:33:31,000
The film grossed $275 million worldwide, approximately the same unadjusted total as the 2001 film of
the same name and more than its 2003 sequel, a figure considered its break-even point.

20
01:38:20,000 --> 01:38:26,000
It received mixed reviews from critics.

21
01:43:15,000 --> 01:43:21,000
A sequel was initially in development with Vikander set to return, but was cancelled in 2022 after
MGM's rights to the Tomb Raider series expired, while Vikander stepped down from the role.

22
01:48:10,000 --> 01:48:16,000
Another reboot film, set to be part of a shared universe that will include a
television series and a video game, is in development at Amazon Studios.

23
01:53:05,000 --> 01:53:11,000
The film explores themes of island, treasure hunt,
remake, female protagonist, heiress.
